# PX4 params for the raptor: the ONE file of the default drone (sim.yaml `px4_params: [raptor]`): collision prevention, the sim-only
# rate gains, the EKF2 lever arms and the GPS-denied sensing mode (baro + LW20 + ZED VIO + PMW3901, no GPS/mag).
# Format: NAME VALUE MAV_PARAM_TYPE (6 INT32, 9 REAL32). Names/ranges checked against the pinned PX4 tag (PX4_TAG, ADR-003).

# --- Collision prevention (Position mode): OFF on the raptor since 2026-10-22 ------------------------------------------
# Kinetix room scans fly close to the walls. PX4 v1.17 applies it in Position mode and to stick nudges in Auto modes, not to
# OFFBOARD setpoints. The ZED bridge still sends obstacle_distance (QGC proximity radar). iris.params keeps CP_DIST 1.5 for
# tests/collision_prevention.py (single_iris); set 1.5 here to bring it back on the raptor.
CP_DIST        -1.0 9   # m. Minimum distance PX4 keeps to an obstacle in Position mode; <= 0 turns collision prevention off
CP_DELAY       0.4  9   # s. Sensor + actuation delay PX4 allows for when braking
CP_GUIDE_ANG   30.0 9   # deg. Tolerance for slipping past an obstacle instead of stopping dead
CP_GO_NO_DATA  0    6   # 0 = allow flight where the map has no data; 1 = forbid it

# --- Rate loop: SIM ONLY. Never load these rows onto the real Pixracer (QGC) -------------------------------------------
# They fit the sim's placeholder plant (Pegasus' Iris thrust curve on the raptor's 0.8 kg / 7x smaller inertia / ~half
# arms), not the real 5" whoop; the real tune is Phase 4 (docs/todo.md). The gazebo-classic_iris gains limit-cycled on this
# body at takeoff (tests/hover_stability.py 2026-10-11: rate std roll 31 / pitch 106 / yaw 96 deg/s). Per unit of PX4 output
# the raptor gets ~2.5x the Iris' roll, ~3x pitch, ~6x yaw angular acceleration, so the Iris values (in the comment) are
# divided by about that: rate std 0.3 deg/s, attitude std < 0.1 deg (PASS).
MC_ROLLRATE_P   0.06    9   # 0.15
MC_ROLLRATE_I   0.08    9   # 0.2
MC_ROLLRATE_D   0.0012  9   # 0.003
MC_PITCHRATE_P  0.05    9   # 0.15
MC_PITCHRATE_I  0.067   9   # 0.2
MC_PITCHRATE_D  0.001   9   # 0.003
MC_YAWRATE_P    0.04    9   # 0.2
MC_YAWRATE_I    0.02    9   # 0.1

# --- Sensor positions (EKF2 lever arms), body FRD, m, from the CoM: the same on the Pixracer --------------------------
# Keep equal to the mounts in docker/sim/assets/vehicles/raptor/raptor.yaml (FLU there: FRD = [x, -y, -z]) and, for the camera, to
# `positional_tracking.initial_base_pose` in docker/zed/zed.yaml. EKF2 removes the rotation-induced motion of each sensor with these;
# they only act when that source is fused (the GPS-denied block below).
EKF2_EV_POS_X   0.1205  9   # ZED Mini (zed_camera_link): FLU [0.1205, 0, 0.0397]. Centred on the real drone (forward offset only);
EKF2_EV_POS_Y   0.0     9   # hover-yaw-step fit over 20 sim flights: camera within 2 mm of these values (docs/vio.md)
EKF2_EV_POS_Z  -0.0397  9
EKF2_RNG_POS_X -0.0645  9   # LW20/C bottom face: FLU [-0.0645, 0.0011, -0.0353]
EKF2_RNG_POS_Y -0.0011  9
EKF2_RNG_POS_Z  0.0353  9
EKF2_OF_POS_X  -0.0645  9   # PMW3901: PLACEHOLDER, shares the LW20's spot (raptor.yaml)
EKF2_OF_POS_Y  -0.0011  9
EKF2_OF_POS_Z   0.0353  9
# Height of the body above the floor when landed, as EKF2 sees it (LW20 reading on the ground ~0.065 + EKF2_RNG_POS_Z). EKF2 uses this
# value in place of every INVALID range sample while landed and at rest. The default 0.01 told EKF2 the floor was 9 cm closer on each
# dropout (the twin: ~6 % of ground samples fall below its 5 cm minimum), and the sample at the takeoff transition left a 9-13 cm
# height offset for the whole flight (2026-10-15, docs/range-flow.md). Real drone: LW20 on the ground + RNG_POS_Z, measured.
EKF2_MIN_RNG    0.10    9

# --- GPS-denied sensing: the real drone's mode (sim and Pixracer) -------------------------------------------------------
#   barometer (on the FC)            -> height REFERENCE
#   LW20/C downward rangefinder      -> height aid + height above the floor; EKF2 learns the baro's bias from it over flat floor
#   ZED Mini VIO (external vision)   -> 3D velocity + yaw (not position, see EKF2_EV_CTRL)
#   PMW3901 optical flow             -> horizontal velocity
# No GPS, no magnetometer (indoors: EV supplies yaw). Lever arms + EKF2_MIN_RNG are above. Needs `services.px4_bridge.odometry.enabled`
# in docker/zed/zed.yaml (sim:). GPS scenarios (Iris) use iris.params + an ekf2_* overlay instead.
#
# Height reference, measured 2026-10-15 on the raptor in Simple Room (docs/range-flow.md "GPS-denied on all sensors"):
#   vision (ekf2_vision): the sim's ZED drifts in z (13-15 cm in 50 s: the SDK tracks without the IMU in the sim) and nothing else
#                         anchors height. The Iris VIO scenario (no ToF/flow) failed vio_flight with 0.85 m of z error this way.
#   range  (2)          : 3.7 cm on a flat floor, but crossing the 0.78 m table edge the drone CLIMBED 0.53 m (0.60 m error):
#                         PX4 warns range/vision references assume a flat floor.
#   baro   (0, chosen)  : 2.1 cm flat, 3.2 cm over the table. Caveat: the sim's baro has no drift or prop wash (Pegasus barometer,
#                         drift 0); on the drone the range aid corrects slow drift, but check prop-wash height jumps near the floor.
# Names/semantics checked against /opt/PX4-Autopilot/src/modules/ekf2/*.yaml (PX4 v1.17.0).

EKF2_GPS_CTRL  0   6   # GPS fusion off
EKF2_MAG_TYPE  5   6   # magnetometer off: EV yaw instead (indoor magnetic fields, and two yaw sources would fight)
EKF2_HGT_REF   0   6   # height reference = baro (0 Baro 1 GPS 2 Range 3 Vision). Reboot-required: applied at SITL boot
EKF2_BARO_CTRL 1   6   # baro fusion on (the default; stated because it is the reference)
EKF2_RNG_CTRL  2   6   # range fusion always on (1 = only low and slow): height aid + terrain; it also learns the baro bias
EKF2_EV_CTRL   12  6   # bit2 3D velocity + bit3 yaw; NOT bit0 horizontal position, NOT bit1 vertical position (the drifting z): see below
EKF2_EV_DELAY  0   9   # ms. Samples are stamped at capture (sim: zed-bridge restamp, zed.yaml; drone: wrapper capture time).
                       # Checked 2026-10-15 (tests/vio_eval.py): residual EV lag vs ground truth 10 ms
EKF2_EVA_NOISE 0.01 9  # EV yaw. PX4 v1.17 floors the yaw variance at max(var, EKF2_EVA_NOISE) (ev_yaw_control.cpp: a std used as a
                       # variance), so the effective yaw std is sqrt(this): 0.01 -> 0.1 rad, the documented default intent. With the
                       # default 0.1 (= 0.32 rad, 18 deg) EKF2's heading lagged the ZED's by ~20 s after each turn while the EV
                       # position kept arriving in the ZED's frame. EV yaw at hover is steady to 0.1 deg (docs/vio.md)
MC_YAWRATE_MAX 60.0 9  # deg/s, every attitude-controlled mode (OFFBOARD, Position sticks; default 200). The sim ZED tracks without
                       # its IMU, and a 90 deg yaw step at the default (325 deg/s peak on the sim's raptor tune) cost it up to 3.6 deg
                       # of yaw each: -8.3 deg after 4 turns, 0.41 m EKF2 error at 2 m from takeoff. At 60 (99 deg/s peak, the sim
                       # tune overshoots): -1.7 deg, 0.11 m. Real camera: IMU-fused, but rotation still blurs features
EKF2_OF_CTRL   1   6   # optical flow fusion on
EKF2_OF_QMIN_GND 1 6   # on the ground use flow only with quality >= 1. The default 0 fuses the twin's quality-0 flow (below its
                       # 8 cm minimum) on the ground: with the ZED down, the at-rest estimate drifted 0.7 m in 3 min (2026-10-15).
                       # With 1, EKF2 holds a constant position at rest instead. It does NOT stop arming without the ZED: at rest
                       # EKF2 always fuses a "valid fake position" (fake_pos_control.cpp), so OFFBOARD arms with no VIO and the
                       # estimate runs off at liftoff. Check the zed-bridge odometry before takeoff (docs/vio.md)
EKF2_OF_DELAY  0   9   # ms. The twin stamps at the end of its integration window (docs/range-flow.md)
#
# EKF2_EV_CTRL 12 (it was 13 until 2026-10-26): EKF2 takes the ZED's velocity and yaw, not its position, because the yaw now comes through the
# zed-bridge's Manhattan compass (docker/zed/zed.yaml `px4_bridge.odometry.heading: manhattan`), which holds it to the room's walls.
# Use the two together: alone, either fails (docs/vio-drift.md).
#   - The compass fixes the heading the sim ZED loses in in-place turns (2-40 deg a slip, 115-209 deg over 320-360 m), but the same
#     tracking events also jump the ZED's position (1.2 m in one 360 deg sweep), which the compass does not see. Fusing the position
#     passes the jumps to EKF2: 4 laps of the drift flight, then aborted at 3 m.
#   - Velocity + yaw without the compass: aborted at 36 m, the heading slips unchecked.
#   - Together (2026-10-26): the 359 m drift flight landed with EKF2 within 1.76 m (0.93 m RMS; the ZED alone was 40 m and 209 deg
#     off), and two Kinetix explore flights stayed within 0.98 / 0.62 m against 1.50 / 2.73 m on the previous setup.
# Sim default since 2026-10-26. Not on the Pixracer until the compass is checked on the real camera (13 = hpos + vel + yaw is the
# value to load there; tests/vio_bench.yaml `ev_position` flies it).
